<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tortola</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tortola is the largest and most populous of the British Virgin Islands, with the capital, Road Town, on its south coast. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> settlers held it before English forces seized it in 1672, and it became the centre of a small colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> plantations worked by enslaved Africans.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tortola.jpg" alt="Tortola" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photo: Henry A-W (Henry aw 23:34, 10 July 2006 (UTC)) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roadtown,_Tortola.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
